# Turns an instruction into something a detector can be asked for.
#
# An open-vocabulary detector takes a short noun phrase with an attribute or two. It cannot parse
# "the mug to the left of the bowl", and it has no notion of which object a sentence is about.
# This is where that gap is closed, by a model that can look at the scene.

string instruction
---
bool ok
string message
# Short noun phrases, one or two attributes each, no relations: what the detector can take.
string[] phrases
# Which of them the instruction is about, so a caller knows what to pick up.
string target_phrase
# The frame the points below index into, and the moment it was captured.
std_msgs/Header header
# Optional, and only as good as the backend: a model that cannot point returns none.
ExemplarPoint[] exemplars
